maximum amount that the price of a futures or options contract may vary either
up or down from the previous day's settlement price. Once the daily limit has
been reached in a particular futures or options market, no trades may be made at
a price beyond the limit. SEE "RISK FACTORS--TRADING AND PERFORMANCE
RISKS--MARKET ILLIQUIDITY MAY CAUSE LESS FAVORABLE TRADE PRICES" ON PAGE 10.


